    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0392" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/4–1745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Embassy to the
                            Department of State
                    </hi><anchor n="31" xml:id="d161-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In connection with the memorandum of the State Department dated March 29 on the
                    question of the invitation of Poland to the Conference at San Francisco, the
                    Embassy of the U.S.S.R., in accordance with instructions of the Soviet
                    Government, has the honor to state that the Soviet Government cannot agree with
                    the arguments of the Government of the United States set forth in the memorandum
                    mentioned. The Soviet Government considers that the inviting of the presently
                    functioning Polish Provisional Government to the Conference at San Francisco not
                    only does not contradict the decisions of the Crimea Conference but is in full
                    accord with the principles of these decisions in as much as the present Polish
                    Provisional Government exercises governmental authority on Polish territory and
                    is fully supported by an overwhelming majority of the Polish people.</p>
                <p>The Soviet Government continues to insist on the necessity of the obligatory
                    participation of the Polish Provisional Government now functioning in Poland in
                    the forthcoming Conference at San Francisco:<anchor n="32" xml:id="d161-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-17">April 17,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d161-f1" n="31" type="source" xml:id="d161-f1-content">
                <p>The Embassy in the Soviet Union was informed of this reply to the Department’s
                    memorandum of March 29 in telegram 920, April 20, 6 p.m. (860C.01/4–1945).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d161-f2" n="32" xml:id="d161-f2-content">
                <p>For press statement concerning the Soviet request and the view of the United
                    States Government on this subject, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 22, 1945, p. 725.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
